# A scout cannot step to a territory its own does not touch.
#
# **`{refused}` says what the rule needed and did not find.** Territory 1 touches 2 and 2 touches
# 3; nothing says 1 touches 3, so `move`'s second clause asks for an adjacency that is not there.

{test name:the-scout-cannot-cross-where-there-is-no-border}

{given}
{territory id:1}
{place id:1 of:1 layer:surface}
{territory id:2}
{place id:2 of:2 layer:surface}
{territory id:3}
{place id:3 of:3 layer:surface}
{adjacency id:1 from:1 to:2}
{adjacency id:2 from:2 to:3}
{scout where:1 moving:1 quantity:1}

{when}
{move what:28 from:1 to:3}

{refused}
{adjacency from:1 to:3}
